    "discussion": {
      "title": "Newton's Method",
      "subtitle": "Pitfalls: Divergence",
      "text": "For $f(x) = x^{1/3}$ the only root is $x = 0$, but the update rule simplifies to $x_{n+1} = x_n - \\frac{x_n^{1/3}}{\\frac{1}{3}x_n^{-2/3}} = -2x_n$. Every iteration flips sides and doubles the distance from the root, so the guesses $0.5, -1, 2, -4, \\dots$ diverge no matter where you start (except exactly at $0$). The culprit is $f'(x) \\to \\infty$ near the root."
    }
